  "rationale": "Hybrid syn-AST scanner (Approach 3) replaces the prior regex-based scanner that produced 568 unique false positives at integration HEAD. The new scanner uses syn::Visit to flag only TRUE direct self-recursion (bare `foo(...)`, `Self::foo(...)`, `self.foo(...)` where the call target equals the enclosing fn's name). Method calls on any other receiver (including trait dispatch on `&dyn ResolverContext`) are correctly NOT flagged. The reduced set of 64 distinct genuinely-self-recursive functions was inspected by hand and classified into three bounding-invariant categories (AST-bounded, DAG-bounded, recursive-descent parser). All 64 carry per-function allow-list entries with phase-report citations. Match key is (file_stem, fn_name) to prevent cross-file collisions from accidentally widening the allow-list. Approach 1 (regex retained, allow-list-only) was rejected because the regex's 568 false positives would have lost discriminating power. Approach 4 (runtime depth-blowup test) was over-scope for a small supplement."
